From: NWA50BE OpenWrt Project <noreply@invalid.example>
Subject: [PATCH] dnsmasq: more post-2.93 fixes and CVE-2026-93010
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only

Add OpenWrt main's 001 and 002 (SIGHUP reload slowdown), twelve upstream
dnsmasq commits newer than 2.93, and a local fix for CVE-2026-93010:

  014 bf80262 TFTP file descriptor leak on a repeated read request
  015 c93e9ce chown/chmod the log file only if it is a regular file
  016 b6b7e5a 1-byte heap overflow in the packet dump checksum
  017 1da5cc2 TCP children close the listening sockets they inherit
  018 7ebe7eb the BSD half of 017 (no effect on Linux)
  019 b518bc4 build fix 017/018 need on non-Linux (no effect on Linux)
  020 7a663fd DNSMASQ_SUPPLIED_HOSTNAME only gets a validated hostname
  021 f031f5b a DS reply without NSEC/NSEC3 no longer loops
  022 a9880c5 a fatal accept() error no longer spins the main loop
  023 baeb743 poll_listen() keeps arrsize until realloc succeeds
  024 bc80b93 queued TCP queries are answered after a stale answer
  025 3a3e7a0 NSEC3 closest encloser check for deeper wildcards
  026 local   ignore DHCP leasequery when no permitted source is set

All apply to 2.93 with no fuzz and no hand resolution. 026 has no
upstream commit: with --leasequery given without an address any host
could read the lease database; it now fails closed and logs once. 200 is
refreshed for 017. The header of 023 drops one trailer line; the code
and the cherry-pick reference are unchanged. dnsmasq is disabled on the
NWA50BE; this keeps the package correct for anyone who enables it.

